        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>A <strong>power of ten</strong> is a number where the leading digit is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1,]</span> and the remaining digits are all zero. </p>",
            "readable_text": "A power of ten is a number where the leading digit is [MATH: 1,] and the remaining digits are all zero.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, the following numbers are all powers of ten:</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, the following numbers are all powers of ten:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10, \\qquad 100, \\qquad 1,000, \\qquad 10,000, \\qquad 100,000, \\qquad \\dots]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 10, \\qquad 100, \\qquad 1,000, \\qquad 10,000, \\qquad 100,000, \\qquad \\dots]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Any power of ten can be written as <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0]</span> where the missing number is equal to the number of zeros in the power of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Any power of ten can be written as [MATH: 0] where the missing number is equal to the number of zeros in the power of [MATH: 10.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, notice that the number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10,000,]</span> which is a power of ten, has a block of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\color{blue}4]</span> zeros:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, notice that the number [MATH: 10,000,] which is a power of ten, has a block of [MATH: \\color{blue}4] zeros:\n[MATH: 4]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, we can write the number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10,000]</span> as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, we can write the number [MATH: 10,000] as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10^{\\color{blue}4}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 10^{\\color{blue}4}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We say that the number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10,000]</span> is expressed in <strong>exponent form.</strong> The number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}4}]</span> is called the <strong>exponent</strong>, and we say that the <strong>base</strong> is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We say that the number [MATH: 10,000] is expressed in exponent form. The number [MATH: {\\color{blue}4}] is called the exponent, and we say that the base is [MATH: 10.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nA power of ten is a number where the leading digit is [MATH: 1,] and the remaining digits are all zero.\n\nContent:\nFor example, the following numbers are all powers of ten:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10, \\qquad 100, \\qquad 1,000, \\qquad 10,000, \\qquad 100,000, \\qquad \\dots]\n\nContent:\nAny power of ten can be written as [MATH: 0] where the missing number is equal to the number of zeros in the power of [MATH: 10.]\n\nContent:\nFor example, notice that the number [MATH: 10,000,] which is a power of ten, has a block of [MATH: \\color{blue}4] zeros:\n[MATH: 4]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, we can write the number [MATH: 10,000] as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10^{\\color{blue}4}]\n\nContent:\nWe say that the number [MATH: 10,000] is expressed in exponent form. The number [MATH: {\\color{blue}4}] is called the exponent, and we say that the base is [MATH: 10.]"
      },
