        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>What is the missing exponent?\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "What is the missing exponent?\n[MATH: 0]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, notice that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10]</span> on the right-hand side has a block of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span> zero:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1 \\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\underset{\\substack{\\uparrow \\[2pt] \\large \\text{one zero}}}{\\color{blue}0}\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!]</span> </p><p>The exponent corresponds to the number of zeros. Therefore, the missing exponent is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}1},]</span> and \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10^{\\color{red}1}=10.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, notice that [MATH: 10] on the right-hand side has a block of [MATH: 1] zero:\n[MATH: 1 \\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\underset{\\substack{\\uparrow \\[2pt] \\large \\text{one zero}}}{\\color{blue}0}\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!]\n\nThe exponent corresponds to the number of zeros. Therefore, the missing exponent is [MATH: {\\color{red}1},] and\n[MATH: 10^{\\color{red}1}=10.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat is the missing exponent?\n[MATH: 0]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, notice that [MATH: 10] on the right-hand side has a block of [MATH: 1] zero:\n[MATH: 1 \\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\underset{\\substack{\\uparrow \\[2pt] \\large \\text{one zero}}}{\\color{blue}0}\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!]\n\nThe exponent corresponds to the number of zeros. Therefore, the missing exponent is [MATH: {\\color{red}1},] and\n[MATH: 10^{\\color{red}1}=10.]"
      },
